Good evening, everyone.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:16.140
What I'd like to do is just give you kind of a brief overview

00:15:18.605 --> 00:15:21.565
of the numbers that we worked with, because a revaluation,

00:15:21.885 --> 00:15:24.045
a mass appraisal revaluation is

00:15:24.445 --> 00:15:26.045
tested by statistics.

00:15:27.565 --> 00:15:29.085
We do the statistics

00:15:29.485 --> 00:15:33.165
based on what the International Association of Assessing Offices

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:34.700
recommend,

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.140
and we do statistics

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:41.260
that the Office of Policy and Management with the State of Connecticut requires us to do.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:49.865
First of all, there were about 53 sales of single family homes in Andover,

00:15:50.185 --> 00:15:53.385
and that represents about 4.2%

00:15:53.385 --> 00:15:54.025
of

00:15:54.425 --> 00:15:56.185
the actual homes in town.

00:15:57.065 --> 00:15:59.625
And that's a historically high number.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:04.030
Typically, we would see it somewhere in the two to 3% range

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.910
in a year that was as less

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:10.510
vibrant as this one is in the real estate field.

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.110
And when we measure

00:16:12.945 --> 00:16:15.025
the validity of a revaluation,

00:16:15.425 --> 00:16:17.345
as I said, we use statistics.

00:16:17.585 --> 00:16:20.865
And one of the major statistics we use is the median

00:16:22.625 --> 00:16:24.545
ratio or median value.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:29.310
And the median is the middle ground between the highest and lowest

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.110
of any data that we're analyzing.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.350
And for this town,

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:40.430
the median ratio, and that ratio is the selling price versus our opinion of market value,

00:16:40.945 --> 00:16:42.785
our median is 95%

00:16:42.785 --> 00:16:47.505
of that market value. And that's typically where we try to be, so that

00:16:48.465 --> 00:16:49.505
we're not

00:16:50.145 --> 00:16:51.985
strictly right at 100%,

00:16:52.225 --> 00:16:56.650
because that 100% number tends to push too many properties over

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.250
the selling price.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:00.250
Another thing to

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:04.250
understand is the median is good at 95%,

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.730
was supposed to be between ninety and one hundred and ten

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:07.770
statistically.

00:17:08.765 --> 00:17:13.405
And another statistic that we use is the coefficient of dispersion.

00:17:14.125 --> 00:17:18.125
It's a big word. What it really measures is how well

00:17:18.765 --> 00:17:27.070
those 53 sales hover around that median. And that's what you want them to do. You want them to be consistent in their level of assessment.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.950
And our coefficient of dispersion

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:34.165
was about under 5%.

00:17:34.725 --> 00:17:36.725
Typically we have to be under 15.

00:17:36.965 --> 00:17:41.285
So again, we met the criteria of both the IAAO and OPM.

00:17:41.925 --> 00:17:43.845
The median selling price

00:17:44.085 --> 00:17:45.685
for a single family home

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:50.290
during this past twelve month period was $280,000

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:56.690
So that's a benchmark for your average or typical home in Andover.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.450
When we look at the lake, there were four sales on the lake,

00:18:02.105 --> 00:18:06.825
and the median selling price there was $650,000

00:18:08.025 --> 00:18:09.945
The low was $4.32

00:18:09.945 --> 00:18:12.425
and the high was 962,000.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:18.230
And this is typical of what we see in waterfront communities.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:23.990
The waterfront typically goes up faster than the remaining part of the town.

